* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux c608b9f (15 Oct 26): Written for QM4 gaps bundle Q-2 (GETLISTV).  The compiler (bcomp, st.getlistv) calls it, as a function, for
*               GETLISTV name TO list.var {SETTING count.var} THEN / ELSE.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* !GETLISTV(name, list.var, count)
*
* The saved list called name in $savedlists becomes the select list variable list.var, and count is set to the number of
* items it holds.  The result is 1 if the list was there (the THEN clause is taken) and 0 if it was not, or $savedlists could
* not be opened (the ELSE clause is taken).  The saved copy is left where it is.  GETLIST does the same into a numbered list
* (_getlist).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

function !getlistv(name, list.var, count)
$catalog !getlistv

   count = 0
   open '$savedlists' to sl.f else return 0
   read saved.list from sl.f, name else return 0

   * SELECTV of a dynamic array in place of a file makes a select list variable from the array
   selectv saved.list to list.var
   count = dcount(saved.list, @fm)
   @selected = count
   return 1
end

* END-CODE
